To refactor the matcher implementation in the Google Mock framework, we will primarily focus on enhancing code modularity and readability while maintaining functionality. This will involve organizing related components more clearly, possibly abstracting logic, and improving documentation within the matcher definitions.

Below is a proposal for a refactor of the matcher classes and functions along with comments on the changes made:

### Refactor Changes
```cpp
// Refactored matcher implementation with improved structure and readability

namespace testing {
namespace gmock_matchers_test {

template <typename T>
struct GreaterThanMatcher : public MatcherInterface<T> {
  explicit GreaterThanMatcher(T rhs) : rhs_(std::move(rhs)) {}

  void DescribeTo(std::ostream* os) const override {
    *os << "is > " << rhs_;
  }

  void DescribeNegationTo(std::ostream* os) const override {
    *os << "is <= " << rhs_;
  }

  bool MatchAndExplain(T lhs, MatchResultListener* listener) const override {
    if (lhs > rhs_) {
      *listener << "which is " << (lhs - rhs_) << " more than " << rhs_;
    } else if (lhs == rhs_) {
      *listener << "which is the same as " << rhs_;
    } else {
      *listener << "which is " << (rhs_ - lhs) << " less than " << rhs_;
    }
    return lhs > rhs_;
  }

 private:
  const T rhs_;
};

// Factory function for creating a GreaterThanMatcher instance
template <typename T>
GreaterThanMatcher<std::decay_t<T>> GreaterThan(T&& rhs) {
  return {std::forward<T>(rhs)};
}

// GTestMatchHelper to provide matcher tests in a parameterized context
class GTestMatcherTestP : public testing::TestWithParam<bool> {
 public:
  template <typename T>
  Matcher<T> GreaterThan(T n) {
    return use_gtest_matcher_ ? GtestGreaterThan(std::move(n))
                               : MakeMatcher(new GreaterThanMatcher<T>(std::move(n)));
  }

 private:
  const bool use_gtest_matcher_ = GetParam();
};

// Matchers and handlers for various match conditions.
template <typename T>
std::string Describe(const Matcher<T>& m) {
  return DescribeMatcher<T>(m);
}

template <typename T>
std::string DescribeNegation(const Matcher<T>& m) {
  return DescribeMatcher<T>(m, true);
}

template <typename MatcherType, typename Value>
std::string Explain(const MatcherType& m, const Value& x) {
  StringMatchResultListener listener;
  ExplainMatchResult(m, x, &listener);
  return listener.str();
}

}  // namespace gmock_matchers_test
}  // namespace testing
```

### Summary of Changes
1. **Cleaner Class Structure**: The `GreaterThanMatcher` class is now simpler and encapsulates the necessary logic directly related to its purpose.
2. **Factory Function**: Introduced a factory function `GreaterThan` that helps to create matcher instances cleanly and efficiently.
3. **Parameter Handling**: Used `std::move` for the right-hand side value (`rhs_`) to enhance performance by avoiding unnecessary copies.
4. **Clarified Method Names**: Kept all original functionality intact while ensuring method names and their usages are clear and descriptive.
5. **Explicit Commenting**: The refactored code includes inline comments to improve understanding and future maintainability.

### Conclusion
This refactor keeps the original functionality intact while enhancing clarity and performance, addressing potential areas for future expansion such as additional matcher types or extended explanations in failure cases. Further iterations can also include more advanced error handling, logging, or extending the matcher capabilities.
